  "title": "Pete V NDE 4900",
  "date": "August 1976",
  "content": "After a night of celebrating while watching the Montréal Olympic games, my friend and I left to go home. He lost control of his white Triumph TR-6 and hit a tree on Lee Boulevard in Baton Rouge. I was unconscious and transported to the emergency room with a concussion, broken nose and broken front teeth. I did not regain consciousness for approximately half an hour. I woke up on emergency room bed, while doctor was stitching lacerations on my nose. However, while I was unconscious at the accident scene, I was in fact hovering above the entire scene below and looking down. I saw the car against the tree, and the ambulance as well as onlookers from the neighborhood and stopped cars. I was in no danger and no pain. I was perfectly aware of what was going on below me, yet in a state of complete tranquility. There was no discomfort, no judgment, and no concerns. My soul left my body and was in a heightened state of consciousness. Ironically, even though I was 'unconscious', my soul was more alert and aware than it could have been merged with my body and mind. Nearly thirty-five years later and I remember it like it was yesterday.",
